course: dictionary
lesson: 13921
title: Leavening: lifting bread and lightening a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Leavening is something that makes a mixture rise and become light. In baking, it is what lifts bread and cakes. Yeast, baking powder and baking soda are all leavenings. «The bread did not rise because the baker forgot the yeast.» Without the leavening, the dough stayed flat and heavy.
explain: Leavening also has a second meaning, used in stories and speeches. A small amount of something, like humour, can lift a heavy or serious piece. «The story was sad, but a leavening of humour made it feel lighter.» The little bit of funny moments made the sad story easier to enjoy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In both meanings, the leavening makes something lighter: a loaf that rises, or a serious story that feels less heavy. If you swap in "something that makes it lighter" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Leavening means something that makes a mixture rise and become light.
fact: Yeast is a leavening: it makes tiny gas bubbles in dough, which push the dough up.
fact: Baking powder and baking soda are also leavenings, and they are used in cakes and scones.
fact: «Leavening» can also mean a small amount of something, like humour, that makes a serious thing lighter.
fact: «Unleavened» means made without leavening, so the bread stays flat. Matzah, eaten at Passover, is unleavened bread.
exercise: «The bread did not rise because the baker forgot the leavening.» What is leavening? | A tool for cutting bread | A kind of flour made from rice | A cold drink | *Something like yeast that makes dough rise
exercise: «Yeast is a leavening: it makes tiny gas bubbles that lift the dough.» What do the yeast bubbles do? | They stop the dough from moving | They turn the dough into sugar | *They lift the dough and make it rise | They make the dough colder
exercise: «The story was sad, but a leavening of humour made it feel lighter.» What does leavening mean here? | *A little something that makes a serious thing lighter | A type of bread with no yeast | A big, heavy meal | A loud noise
test: «Unleavened bread has no yeast in it, so it stays flat.» What does unleavened mean? | *Made without leavening, so it stays flat | Very tasty | Made with eggs | Burnt on the outside
test: In a Bible story, leaven means yeast, the thing that makes dough rise. What is leaven here? | A bread knife | A type of sheep | *Yeast, the thing that makes dough rise | A kind of meat
exam: «Baking powder and baking soda are leavenings, so the cake rises.» What makes the cake rise? | Sugar | *Baking powder or baking soda | Icing | The oven door
